      "writtenOn": "2022-05-12T21:01:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a pretty hacky approach, and permits certain things that aren\u0027t allowed in GLSL - specifically splitting the directive line. (Technically that\u0027s true for how we handle extension directives as well). It\u0027s not terrible - we accept a strict superset of legal GLSL in that regard (eg, you can still put comments before the #version, just no other directives or declarations).",
      "revId": "08603c5bbc7a0facf6af7255c67e48d73a804080",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
